# Toro Platform Overview

## Stack

- **Language**: Go 1.25 (primary), Python (NATS worker)
- **APIs**: GraphQL (gqlgen), REST (net/http with Go 1.22+ routing)
- **Database**: PostgreSQL 18 (TimescaleDB), accessed via **sqlc** (type-safe SQL → Go)
- **Migrations**: Goose (sequential SQL in `sql/schema/`)
- **Messaging**: NATS JetStream (3-node cluster, at-least-once delivery)
- **Cache**: Ristretto (in-memory L1, 100MB) + Redis (distributed L2, revocation)
- **Auth**: Ed25519 JWT, Argon2id password hashing, Redis token blacklist
- **AI/ML**: OpenAI embeddings → Pinecone vector DB
- **Integrations**: QuickBooks Online, Plaid, Stripe
- **Infra**: Docker Compose, Nginx reverse proxy, `toro-net` network

## Repository Layout

```
go/cmd/          — Executable services (gate, graphql, ws, sync, cdc-worker, protocol, analytics)
go/internal/     — Private packages (auth, api, store, database, queue, services, config, resilience)
go/qbo/          — QuickBooks Online client
tap/             — Toro Agent Protocol submodule (separate go.mod)
sql/schema/      — Goose migration files
sql/queries/     — sqlc query definitions
container/       — Dockerfiles and docker-compose configs
python-worker/   — Python NATS subscriber
```

## Multi-Tenancy Model

Hierarchical entity tree: `Apex CPA → Sub CPA → Client`. Row-Level Security enforced via `SET LOCAL app.current_entity` in transactions. Entity descendant tree resolved once per request, passed as `authorized_entity_ids` to queries.

## Key Commands

- `make up` — start dev stack
- `make sqlc` — regenerate sqlc + run migrations
- `make test` — `go test ./...`
- `make migrate` — run Goose migrations
